<%#
  What the tints and icons in the table mean: one question and its answer,
  rendered inside the page's About This Report list.

  Every sample is rendered through the same partials the rows use, so the
  legend cannot drift from the table it explains.
%>
<dt>What do the colors and icons mean?</dt>
<dd>
  <%# A grid rather than a wrapping row: six sample/meaning pairs flowing freely
      run together, and the plain-text "Qualified" sample has no badge edge to
      mark where it ends. %>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
    <div class="flex-center-gap-2">
      <%= render "summary_value", value: "Claimed", status: AccessDocument::CLAIMED %>
      <span class="text-stone-muted">Ready to use this year</span>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-center-gap-2">
      <%= render "summary_value", value: "Banked", status: AccessDocument::BANKED %>
      <span class="text-stone-muted">Saved for a later year</span>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-center-gap-2">
      <%= render "summary_value", value: "Submitted", status: AccessDocument::SUBMITTED %>
      <span class="text-stone-muted">Sent to the ticket vendor</span>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-center-gap-2">
      <%= render "summary_value", value: "Qualified", status: nil %>
      <span class="text-stone-muted">Earned, not claimed yet</span>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-center-gap-2">
      <%= render "summary_value", value: nil %>
      <span class="text-stone-muted">None of this kind held</span>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-center-gap-2">
      <%= render "summary_missing" %>
      <span class="text-stone-muted">Needs an arrival date</span>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-center-gap-2">
      <%= render "summary_error", error: "RAD-0000" %>
      <span class="text-stone-muted">Something to look into</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</dd>
